decision=observed
identity=prozess-reflexion-03
intent=Festhalten, was der erste Betrieb über den Orchestrator gemessen hat: Wünsche, Runden, Ablehnungen, Kosten, und was die Ablehnungen verursacht hat.
scope=Night of 2026-11-25 to 2026-11-26, 16 jobs job-ticket-003 to job-ticket-023 that the orchestrator planned from requests in plain words. Numbers are read from the records of these jobs. Costs are list prices; the calls ran on a subscription. The requests were written, approved, answered and landed by the agent claude-fable on the instruction of the user. The work inside the jobs was done by an Opus 5.5 worker, the gates by Savant or by a Sonnet 5.5 agent.
measured_jobs=16 jobs: 9 sessions on the repository taik and 7 changes to the product ansicht. 15 ended accepted, 1 was closed by command after 5 rejected rounds. 9 were accepted in their first round.
measured_cost=27.26 USD at list price for all rounds, analyses and questions of the 16 jobs, without the calls of the orchestrator and the gate authors. The closed job job-ticket-008 alone took 9.24 USD and 645 s of worker time.
measured_gate_author=The same request ran twice. job-ticket-008: gate written by an author without access to the repository, 5 rounds rejected, 9.24 USD, closed. job-ticket-009: gate written by an author who read the repository first, accepted in round 1, 1.14 USD. This is one pair, not a sample. It is the observation that led to round 30 of job-backend.
causes_of_rejected_rounds=job-ticket-003: 3 rounds, all three by faults of the Factory (sandbox of the gate without mktemp and null device, no cargo in the search path of the service), none by the work. job-ticket-006: 4 rounds by a name that an old gate forbade and whose finding did not name it; the analysis written by the Factory named it. job-ticket-008: 5 rounds by an unsatisfiable gate.
causes_of_rejected_promotions=4 of 14 promotions of merged session work were rejected by the installed binary (rounds 34, 36, 37, 41 of job-backend): once Clippy, three times a test that needs the sandbox and that the gate of the session could not run. Each was corrected by the agent after one reply in its ticket.
questions_of_agents=The worker asked the user 2 times (job-ticket-003), both times because a finding of the gate showed no cause. The gate author declined 2 requests with a reason that was right (ticket-011 not checkable in the gate's sandbox, ticket-015 contradicted an existing test). The orchestrator asked back once (ticket-021).
what_changed_the_boundary=By hand, each as a round of its own in job-backend: the author of a session gate reads the repository (30), a product change gets a check that must fail on the current source (39). Since round 39 the gate of the product ansicht grew by 3 checks from 3 jobs.
not_shown=Whether the Factory proposes useful work by itself. Every request of this night came from the agent. G-03, I-01 and I-03 of the specification stay not established: there is no baseline run of the same requests without the orchestrator.
limitation=The numbers come from one night, one repository and one worker model. A session agent has no shell and cannot build or test; the two-step check (gate of the job, then the whole suite at promotion) is the consequence and cost 4 promotion rounds.
continuation=Let the gate of a session run the test targets that need a sandbox, or give the promotion finding back to the job without an agent in between. Measure the same requests with and without a reading gate author on more than one pair before claiming an effect.
end
